<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104327" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόπαζος</span></b> , ὁ, a gem of
		green hue (<i><span class="en">
			Plin.
			<u>HN</u>
			37.107
		</span></i>), hence prob. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>chrysolite</i> or <i>peridot,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				6.329
			</span></i> (Leon.<i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				3.7.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				1121
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>L.</u>
				278
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόπαζον</span></b> , τό, Eust.ad <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
			</span></i> l.c.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοπάζιον</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				28.17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ps.</u>
				118(119).127
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				16.4.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				3.39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Apoc.</u>
				21.20
			</span></i>:—Pliny (<u>HN</u> l.c.) gives the name of
				<i>topazon</i> (v.l.
			<i>topazium</i>) to two varieties. (From the Trogodyte language
			acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
			</span></i> l. c.; perh. the same as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταβάσιος.</span>)</div>
